<article class="env-lemma" id="0GL1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GL1">Lemma <span data-tag="0GL1">21.20.9</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. For $L$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ and $K$ in $D(\mathcal{O})$ we have $j_!L \otimes _\mathcal {O}^\mathbf {L} K = j_!(L \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ U}^\mathbf {L} K|_ U)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Represent $L$ by a complex of $\mathcal{O}_ U$-modules and $K$ by a K-flat complexe of $\mathcal{O}$-modules and apply Modules on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0E8I" data-tag="0E8I">18.27.9</a>. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>